# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores LF for every text file. `eol=lf` additionally pins the
# *working tree* to LF on every platform, so a Windows checkout cannot quietly
# reintroduce CRLF the way it did before this file existed: a Git for Windows
# default of core.autocrlf=true hides the drift locally, but anything that
# reads the bytes directly - a Linux CI checkout, an editor that preserves
# per-line endings, a patch tool - sees it.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary content and leaves it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows tooling that expects CRLF. Normalized to LF in the repository and
# checked out as CRLF. Nothing outside third_party/ currently matches these;
# the rules exist so that adding a build script under tools/ does the right
# thing without anyone having to remember this file.
*.bat             text eol=crlf
*.cmd             text eol=crlf
*.sln             text eol=crlf
*.props           text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj         text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj.filters text eol=crlf

# Binary content Git must never inspect, diff or convert. `text=auto` would
# classify all of these correctly on its own; naming them keeps the common
# cases off the content-sniffing path entirely.
#
# Deliberately absent: *.obj and *.mtl. Those are Wavefront model *text* here,
# not Windows object files, and must stay under the rules above.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.fbx  binary
*.blend binary
*.glb  binary
*.bin  binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.ogg  binary
*.wav  binary
*.flac binary
*.opus binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.jar  binary
*.lib  binary
*.unitypackage binary

# Vendored dependencies stay byte-exact with upstream, so that re-vendoring a
# release produces a diff about the release rather than about line endings.
# Deeper .gitattributes files still win inside their own subtree, which is how
# third_party/imgui keeps its CRLF Visual Studio projects.
#
# This must stay below the rules above: within one .gitattributes file, the
# last matching line wins.
third_party/** -text

# Vendored asset pack shipped with CRLF licence files. Left byte-exact for the
# same reason as third_party/, and quoted because the path contains spaces.
"assets/Kenney Game Assets All-in-1 3.5.0/**" -text
